<title>SINGAPORE: TIBS Holdings 1996 net plunges into the red.</title>
<headline>TIBS Holdings 1996 net plunges into the red.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit/loss	    (loss)  5.14  vs   6.96 (gain)</p>
<p>Dividend (percent)		   5.00  vs   9.50</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	  (loss) 11.30  vs  15.28</p>
<p>    Turnover			     156.40  vs 143.69</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	3.11  vs   2.70</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   2.84  vs   1.20</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    28.43  vs  15.89</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.20  vs   0.22</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit/loss	(loss)  6.69  vs  11.25  (gain)</p>
<p>Tax					0.45  vs   4.42</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (gain)  1.80  vs   0.09 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			0.00  vs   0.72 (loss)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: July 17, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: July 8, 1997</p>
<p>Note - TIBS Holdings Ltd said its results were hit by competition from Singapore's Mass Rapid Transit rail network, higher operational costs and lower margins. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
